Package: PhysioStream
Title: Governed Real-Time Streams for Physiological Data
Version: 0.9.4
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Yusuke",
           family = "Matsui",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mail.to.matsui@gmail.com")
Description: Provides validated stream metadata, source and sink contracts,
    a bounded single-producer/single-consumer ring buffer, deterministic
    in-process loopback streams, capability-gated Lab Streaming Layer
    inlets and outlets, marker-event capture, governed Extensible Data
    Format read/write, and conversion of buffered physiological samples
    to PhysioExperiment objects, with explicit robust clock-offset, drift,
    jitter, multi-stream synchronization, transactional causal processing
    pipelines, explicit backpressure, monotonic latency measurement, and
    governed loopback, MQTT, and TTL stimulation-command outlets with
    arm, dead-man, maximum, duplicate-ID, and refractory interlocks,
    plus causal EMG-onset, EEG-ERD, and phase-target detectors bound to
    commit-before-stimulation closed-loop session control and provenance,
    with a bounded live biofeedback scope and marker-anchored video-time
    synchronization.
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2),
    PhysioExperiment (>= 2.0.0)
